# .bedigital-visual-tests/recipe.env — sourced by scripts/sandbox.sh.
# Commit this file. Plain KEY=VALUE only (it is `source`d by bash).

# The compose service that serves the web app the browser will hit. (required)
APP_SERVICE=frontend

# The port the app listens on INSIDE its container. (required)
# The sandbox publishes this on an ephemeral host port — never hard-code the host side.
APP_PORT=3000

# Path polled on the published port until it returns 200 before the browser drives. (default /)
HEALTH_PATH=/api/health

# Space-separated lockfile globs. Their combined hash tags the base image and
# decides when a re-onboard is needed. List EVERY lockfile that affects deps. (required)
LOCKFILES="frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml backend/uv.lock"

# OPTIONAL: an existing repo compose to layer the sanitizing override on top of.
# Leave unset for the self-contained path (Dockerfile.base + Dockerfile.sandbox).
# BASE_COMPOSE=docker-compose.yml

# ---- Review mode (v2 adversarial brain) -------------------------------------

# Stateful services `sandbox.sh reset` recreates between missions. (default: postgres)
# Space-separated. Only matters for review mode.
# DATA_SERVICES="postgres redis"

# OPTIONAL custom reseed command for `reset` — needed when the DB uses a NAMED
# volume (SHAPE A) so dropping the container doesn't wipe it, or when seeding
# runs via a migrate/seed profile. $COMPOSE (full `docker compose -p <proj> -f…`)
# and $PROJ are provided. Leave unset for SHAPE B (anonymous volume + initdb seed).
# RESET_CMD='$COMPOSE --profile seed run --rm seed'

# Model policy for review mode. IDs are current-as-of and overridable.
# Planner (reads the diff, generates missions) = the agent running the skill —
# launch it under a strong model. Delegates (drive the browser per mission) are
# spawned as DELEGATE_MODEL subagents.
PLANNER_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
DELEGATE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# ---- Auth (v5) — arrive able to log in --------------------------------------
# Default path: the seed creates this user ALREADY CONFIRMED and the delegate logs
# in through the app's REAL login form. These are THROWAWAY, sandbox-only creds —
# safe to commit. NEVER put a real user's credentials here. Leave the whole block
# unset for apps with no auth (behavior is then unchanged).
#
# `sandbox.sh up` echoes the set keys (like SANDBOX_URL) so the planner hands them
# to each delegate; the delegate uses ONLY these, never real creds.
# TEST_USER=tester@sandbox.local
# TEST_PASSWORD=sandbox-only-pw
# LOGIN_PATH=/login
# POST_LOGIN_PATH=/            # where a good login lands (delegate asserts this)

# ---- DB seeding (v5) — populate the throwaway sandbox DB --------------------
# Strategy:
#   initdb      (default) — the Postgres image's /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d only.
#               No MIGRATE_CMD/SEED_CMD needed. This is the pre-v5 behavior.
#   migrations  — run MIGRATE_CMD (the repo's migration tool) to build the schema,
#               then optional SEED_CMD, IN-CONTAINER against the throwaway DB.
#   synthetic   — run SEED_CMD (fake data + the confirmed TEST_USER) in-container.
# (Phase 3 will add a sanitized real-data snapshot strategy — not yet implemented.)
#
# MIGRATE_CMD / SEED_CMD run via `docker compose run --rm` on the sandbox network —
# NOT on the host. DATABASE_URL inside the sandbox points at the throwaway local
# Postgres; a real/VPS/cloud DB URL must NEVER be injected into the sandbox.
# For a remote/VPS-Postgres app, replicate LOCALLY: point the app's DATABASE_URL at
# a throwaway postgres service in sandbox.compose.yml, then migrate+seed it here.
#
# SEED_SERVICE: the compose service whose image runs the seed (default: APP_SERVICE —
# the app image usually carries the migration CLI as a dependency). Set a dedicated
# seed service only if the tooling isn't in the app image.
# SEED_STRATEGY=migrations
# SEED_SERVICE=frontend
# MIGRATE_CMD=npx prisma migrate deploy
# SEED_CMD=node scripts/seed.js

# ---- Supabase apps (v5 Phase 2) ---------------------------------------------
# If the app authenticates against Supabase, run a LOCAL Supabase stack in the
# sandbox instead of pointing at the real project. Use templates/supabase.sandbox.
# compose.example.yml + templates/supabase/* and seed a confirmed user via the
# admin API — it reuses the SAME seed hook above:
#   DATA_SERVICES="db auth rest gateway"
#   SEED_STRATEGY=synthetic
#   SEED_SERVICE=frontend
#   SEED_CMD="node scripts/seed-supabase-user.mjs"
# Full playbook (well-known dev keys, the NEXT_PUBLIC/ephemeral-port trap →
# server-side auth, reset reseeds auth): reference/supabase.md.

# ---- Sanitized real-data snapshot (v5 Phase 3) — OPT-IN, sensitive -----------
# Pull a SCOPED, READ-ONLY, PII-MASKED slice of a real DB into the sandbox at
# runtime. Real data + a published Artifact = GDPR/leak risk → masking is
# NON-NEGOTIABLE. READ reference/snapshot.md before enabling. Note: SOURCE_DB_URL
# is INJECTED AT RUNTIME (SOURCE_DB_URL=... bash sandbox.sh up) and must NEVER be
# committed here or in the compose.
# SEED_STRATEGY=snapshot
# SEED_SERVICE=frontend
# MIGRATE_CMD="npx prisma migrate deploy"
# SEED_CMD="node scripts/snapshot-and-mask.mjs"
# SNAPSHOT_CONFIG=.bedigital-visual-tests/snapshot.config.json
# (optional) SNAPSHOT_DUMP=... — writes ONLY masked data; the path MUST be gitignored.
